Completion
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/signal_array]

FIXME(wonder): The crew finishes the pylon. Veran checks the cable connections one by one. Chorik fits the top cross-piece. Baret rolls up the rest circle and stows the kit. Richard reads the activation sequence from a laminated card he keeps in his pocket. Twenty minutes of focused work. The four of them work the way the crew of any well-run job works. When the last bolt is tight Richard turns the key on the housing.

FIXME(dread): There is a click. Something cycles up inside the housing. The pylon is live.

FIXME(horror): The weight is immediate. It is not pain. It is purpose. Blueprints unroll in your mind: schematics with part numbers for components you have never seen and now understand the function of, coordinates for the next site east, material quantities, scheduling margins. The full weight of a job that is organized and waiting and makes complete sense.

FIXME(horror): You push against it. The offer-language was wrong. There is no offer. The signal is doing to you what was done to the four of them around the housing. It is replacing the parts of you that hold your name with parts that hold schematics. It is hostile and fast and moving inside your head with the unhurried confidence of something that has done this before. You push back against it with everything you are and do not know yet whether it is enough.

FIXME(dread): You surface. The crew is somewhere else behind the eyes. They are present in body. They are not coordinated yet. The activator housing is at the base of the pylon, closed and latched. The window will not stay open.

# GAP (load-bearing): the bibles called for a save-shaped resist
# roll here, separate from the act picker below. Deferred from the
# skeleton pending author decision on the signal_caught fragment
# quality. If wanted, drop a single picker choice (Cunning per the
# bibles, or Bushcraft) between the body and the act/clear choices
# below, with both branches +open-ing into a small Window.enc file
# that hosts the fork.

choices:

* Move on the housing = Get to the activator
    FIXME(action): You move on the housing. The latch plate is bolted to the bedrock and will need force to break. The crew is on the work side of the housing, not coordinated yet. Veran is the closest.
    @if check combat correct:rush wrong:outlast {
        FIXME(action): You commit the moment you decide. You drive the heel of your hand against the latch plate. The plate bends. You strip the housing open, pull the activator unit out, and break it across your knee. The signal cuts. The pylon goes dark behind you.
        +open "Aftermath"
    } @else {
        FIXME(action): You hold a beat to read the moment. The beat is too long. Veran's hand is on your shoulder before you set yourself. He is not aggressive. He is firm.
        +open "Grabbed"
    }

* Get clear of the pylon = Put distance between yourself and the signal
    FIXME(horror): You stumble back from the housing. Each step you take from the pylon, the signal thins by a degree, and your head clears by the same degree. By the time you are forty paces out the schematics have receded to a low hum at the back of your skull. You know now not to get close to one of these again.
    FIXME(dread): You watch from the rocks at a safe distance as the crew finishes their transition. They collect their tools with the synchronized economy of people who know exactly where they are going and why. They form up and start east down the mesa road toward the next build site, wherever that is. You watch them go and there is nothing you can do about it.
    +finish_dungeon
    +add_level
